@startuml fig-2-5-1-class-reconcile
' SDS Figure II-2.5.1 — Class diagram: self-healing reconciliation (level-triggered backstops)
' NOTE: section heading in the .docx currently duplicates 2.4 ("Idle Parking &
' Preemption"); it should read "Self-Healing Reconciliation".
' Verified against wes/src/opentcs/kernel-event-listener.service.ts,
' vehicle-state.store.ts and wes/src/cargo/leg-reconcile.service.ts.
' Render: java -jar plantuml.jar -charset UTF-8 -tpng fig-2-5-1-class-reconcile.puml
!include _style.iuml

class KernelEventListenerService <<ACL, SSE>> {
  +onApplicationBootstrap(): void
  +onApplicationShutdown(): void
  -connect(): void
  -seedStore(): void
  -reconcileVehicleStates(): void  «heartbeat 5s»
  -handleTO(payload): void
  -handleVehicle(payload): void
}

class LegReconcileService <<Service, backstop>> {
  +run(): void
  -reconcileTask(task): void
  -expectedLeg(task): {leg, orderName}?
}

class VehicleStateStore <<ACL, in-memory>> {
  +get(name): KernelVehicleState?
  +getAll(): KernelVehicleState[]
  +set(name, state): void
  +setConnected(value): void
  +isConnected(): boolean
}

class KernelApiService <<ACL>> {
  +getVehicleStates(): KernelVehicleState[]
  +getTransportOrderState(name): string
}

class TransportTaskService <<Service, choke-point>> {
  +changeStatus(task, to, log): TransportTaskEntity
}

class EventEmitter2

VehicleStateStore -[hidden]- KernelApiService
TransportTaskService -[hidden]- EventEmitter2

KernelEventListenerService --> VehicleStateStore
KernelEventListenerService --> KernelApiService
KernelEventListenerService --> EventEmitter2
LegReconcileService --> VehicleStateStore
LegReconcileService --> KernelApiService
LegReconcileService --> TransportTaskService
LegReconcileService --> EventEmitter2

note bottom of LegReconcileService
  Runs as the first engine of every flush. Re-confirms each
  live task's expected leg against the kernel and either
  re-fires fms.transport-order.finished (FINISHED) or fails
  the task (FAILED / UNROUTABLE).
end note

note right of KernelEventListenerService
  Correctness never depends on an in-process event surviving:
  the 5s heartbeat re-seeds VehicleStateStore and re-emits
  fms.vehicle.available from authoritative kernel state.
end note

@enduml
